{
  "name": "RobotFrameworkAIO.Exercise_01",
  "title": "Exercise 01: Building Testsuites",
  "summary": "Write a Robot Framework test suite using RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement and run it with p1.check().",
  "introduction": [
    "In this exercise you will create a Robot Framework test suite that uses the TestsuitesManagement library.",
    "Assign your robot script to the `robot_code` variable and call `p1.check()` to execute and validate it."
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "title": "Practice 1: Simple test suite with TestsuitesManagement",
      "prompt": [
        "Create a Robot Framework test suite script and assign it to the `robot_code` variable.",
        "The suite must import `RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement` with alias `tm` and call `tm.testsuite_setup` as `Suite Setup`.",
        "Add a test case that logs the `${CONFIG}[Maximum_version]` and `${CONFIG}[Project]` configuration values.",
        "Call `p1.check()` to execute the robot script and verify that all tests pass."
      ],
      "starter_code": [
        "robot_code = \"\"\"",
        "*** Settings ***",
        "",
        "Library    RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement    WITH NAME    tm",
        "",
        "Suite Setup    tm.testsuite_setup",
        "",
        "*** Test Cases ***",
        "Test Case practice-01",
        "    [documentation]    practice-01",
        "    Log    <your log statement here>    console=yes",
        "\"\"\"",
        "p1.check()"
      ],
      "hint": [
        "Use the `*** Settings ***` section to import the library and configure `Suite Setup`:",
        "",
        "```",
        "Library    RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement    WITH NAME    tm",
        "Suite Setup    tm.testsuite_setup",
        "```",
        "",
        "Then in `*** Test Cases ***`, use the `Log` keyword with `console=yes` to print the `${CONFIG}` values.",
        "",
        "Access config values with `${CONFIG}[key_name]` syntax."
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here is a complete solution:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "robot_code = \"\"\"",
        "*** Settings ***",
        "",
        "Library    RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement    WITH NAME    tm",
        "",
        "Suite Setup    tm.testsuite_setup",
        "",
        "*** Test Cases ***",
        "Test Case practice-01",
        "    [documentation]    practice-01",
        "    Log    Maximum_version : ${CONFIG}[Maximum_version]    console=yes",
        "    Log    Project : ${CONFIG}[Project]    console=yes",
        "\"\"\"",
        "p1.check()",
        "```"
      ],
      "success_message": "Correct. The robot test suite ran successfully.",
      "failure_message": "The robot suite did not pass. Check the robot output above for details.",
      "tags": ["robot", "testsuite", "TestsuitesManagement"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "title": "Practice 2: Test suite with a custom configuration file",
      "prompt": [
        "In this practice you define a custom configuration file in JSONP format and pass it to the robot test suite via the `${config_file}` robot variable.",
        "",
        "Steps:",
        "1. The `json_config` variable holds the JSONP configuration content — it is already written to `config_file_path` for you.",
        "2. Build `robot_code` as an **f-string** so that `${config_file}` is set from `config_file_path` in the `*** Variables ***` section.",
        "3. Import `RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement` and add `tm.testsuite_setup` as `Suite Setup`.",
        "4. Add a test case that checks the configuration values.",
        "5. Call `p2.check()` to execute the suite and verify all tests pass."
      ],
      "starter_code": [
        "json_config = \"\"\"\n{\n    ...\n}\"\"\"",
        "config_file_path = './learningtools/examples/RobotFrameworkAIO/config/practice2_config.jsonp'",
        "with open(config_file_path, 'w') as f:",
        "    f.write(json_config)",
        "",
        "robot_code = f\"\"\"",
        "*** Variables ***",
        "${config_file}   {config_file_path}",
        "",
        "*** Settings ***",
        "<Import testsuites management library>",
        "",
        "<Suite Setup>    <Keyword to setup the test suite>",
        "",
        "*** Test Cases ***",
        "<Test cases go here>",
        "\"\"\"",
        "p2.check()"
      ],
      "hint": [
        "Set the variable `config_file` under `*** Variables ***` to the path of the JSONP config file `config_file_path`.",
        "Import the `RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement` library and configure `Suite Setup`",
        "",
        "```",
        "Library    RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement    WITH NAME    tm",
        "Suite Setup    tm.testsuite_setup",
        "```",
        "",
        "Then in `*** Test Cases ***`, use the `Should Be Equal` keyword with `console=yes` to check the configuration values.",
        "",
        "Access config values with `${<parameter_name>}` syntax."
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here is a complete solution:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "robot_code = f\"\"\"",
        "*** Variables ***",
        "${config_file}   {config_file_path}",
        "",
        "*** Settings ***",
        "Library    RobotFramework_TestsuitesManagement    WITH NAME    tm",
        "",
        "Suite Setup    tm.testsuite_setup",
        "",
        "*** Test Cases ***",
        "Test Case practice-02",
        "    [documentation]    practice-02",
        "    Should Be Equal    ${{robot_variable_1}}    ABC",
        "    Should Be Equal    ${{robot_variable_2}}    ${{25}}",
        "\"\"\"",
        "p2.check()",
        "```"
      ],
      "success_message": "Correct. The robot test suite with the custom config file ran successfully.",
      "failure_message": "The robot suite did not pass. Check the robot output above for details.",
      "tags": ["robot", "testsuite", "TestsuitesManagement", "config"]
    }
  ]
}
